From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:26:11 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] tccasm, i386-asm: forward labels in symbol differences are
 constants first

"leal rva(gdt)(%ebp), %eax" (rva(X) = X - startup_32) and ".quad gdt -
gdt64" in the kernel's compressed head_64.S subtract labels of one
section where the first one is defined later in the file.  Pass two
knows both, but the PC-relative conversion ("sym - label of this
section") was tried before the two-pass resolution and produced an
absolute relocation (R_X86_64_32/64), which the -pie link of the
decompressor refuses - and for .quad the wrong value.  The difference
of two labels of one section is now resolved to a constant whenever
pass two knows them, before the PC-relative forms; pass one defers.

A parenthesized displacement expression keeps its pcrel flag (it was
cleared with the "(%reg)" case), and ".quad sym - label" of symbols in
different sections gets R_X86_64_PC64.

The compressed head_64.o now has only PC32/PLT32 relocations like GNU
as's object; the PC-relative data test file still links to GNU as's
bytes; make test and the .code16/.code32/.code64 encoding checks pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 i386-asm.c |  4 +++-
 tccasm.c   | 18 ++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/i386-asm.c b/i386-asm.c
index 0ad86cc..626edce 100644
--- a/i386-asm.c
+++ b/i386-asm.c
@@ -470,12 +470,14 @@ static void parse_operand(TCCState *s1, Operand *op)
                 unget_tok('(');
                 op->e.v = 0;
                 op->e.sym = NULL;
+                op->e.pcrel = 0;
             } else {
+                /* a PC-relative value ("rva(gdt)(%ebp)" = (gdt - startup_32))
+                   keeps its pcrel flag, like an unparenthesized one */
                 unget_tok('(');
                 asm_expr(s1, &e);
                 op->e = e;
             }
-	    op->e.pcrel = 0;
         }
         if (tok == '(') {
 	    unsigned int type = 0;
diff --git a/tccasm.c b/tccasm.c
index 784ea54..c371855 100644
--- a/tccasm.c
+++ b/tccasm.c
@@ -275,6 +275,16 @@ ST_FUNC void gen_addr64(int r, Sym *sym, int64_t c)
 
 ST_FUNC void gen_expr64(ExprValue *pe)
 {
+#ifdef TCC_TARGET_X86_64
+    if (pe->pcrel) {
+        /* ".quad sym - label": pe->v is -<label offset> (gen_expr32's
+           convention), the relocation is relative to this field */
+        greloca(cur_text_section, pe->sym, ind, R_X86_64_PC64, pe->v + ind);
+        gen_le32(0);
+        gen_le32(0);
+        return;
+    }
+#endif
     gen_addr64(pe->sym ? VT_SYM : 0, pe->sym, pe->v);
 }
 #endif
@@ -615,6 +625,12 @@ static inline void asm_expr_sum(TCCState *s1, ExprValue *pe)
 		    /* we also accept defined symbols in the same section */
 		    pe->v += (int)(esym1->st_value - esym2->st_value);
 		    pe->sym = NULL;
+		} else if (asm_pass_resolve(pe, &e2)) {
+		    /* labels defined later: the difference of two labels of
+		       one section is a constant also when one of them comes
+		       later (".quad gdt - gdt64", "leal rva(gdt)(%ebp)" in
+		       the kernel's compressed head), so this is tried before
+		       the PC-relative forms below; the first pass defers */
 		} else if (esym2 && esym2->st_shndx == cur_text_section->sh_num) {
 		    /* When subtracting a defined symbol in current section
 		       this actually makes the value PC-relative.  */
@@ -629,8 +645,6 @@ static inline void asm_expr_sum(TCCState *s1, ExprValue *pe)
 		    pe->v += (int)(0 - v2);
 		    pe->pcrel = 1;
 		    e2.sym = NULL;
-		} else if (asm_pass_resolve(pe, &e2)) {
-		    /* labels defined later in an inline asm statement */
 		} else {
 cannot_relocate:
 		    tcc_error("invalid operation with label");
